<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch sugar beet area seen unchanged from 1996.</title>
<headline>Dutch sugar beet area seen unchanged from 1996.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch sugar beet plantings are due to start at the end of this month and cover an area roughly equal to last season's 116,000 hectares, the director of the Dutch Institute for Sugar Research said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Frans Tijink told Reuters the plantings could take between two and seven weeks to complete depending on weather conditions. He described the weather in the run-up to the planting season as &quot;reasonable&quot; for the crop.</p>
<p>He added the IRS would again use computerised beet forecasts and not reports from the field to monitor the crop's progress. --Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
